<title>UK: Candover to buy Barclay's Camden.</title>
<headline>Candover to buy Barclay's Camden.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>British investment firm Candover Investments said on Tuesday it had backed the management buyout of Camden Motors Ltd, the motor retailer belonging to Barclays Bank Plc.  </p>
<p>Camden, as a wholly-owned subsidiary of Barclays, operates a multi-franchise network in the UK covering Ford, Vauxhall, Peugeot, Rover, Renault, Nissan, Volkswagen, Audi and Honda.</p>
<p>Camden mainly operates in the Midlands and south east with over 450 people at nine UK locations.</p>
<p>The new charirman of Camden would be Geoffrey Whalen, former chairman of Peugeot UK.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44-171-542 7717</p>
